# Business Exceptions — TokenRealty

## Standard exceptions

| Exception | HTTP | ProblemDetail type |
|-----------|------|-------------------|
| `ResourceNotFoundException` | 404 | `/errors/not-found` |
| `ConflictException` | 409 | `/errors/conflict` |
| `ValidationException` | 422 | `/errors/business-rule` |
| `MethodArgumentNotValidException` | 400 | `/errors/validation` |

All services use `GlobalExceptionHandler` returning RFC 7807 `ProblemDetail` with `timestamp` property.

## Raise helpers

Do not scatter `throw new ValidationException(...)` — use private helpers in services:

```java
// BAD
if (!listing.isActive()) {
    throw new ValidationException("Listing is not active");
}

// GOOD
if (!listing.isActive()) {
    raiseValidation("Listing is not active");
}

private static void raiseValidation(String message) {
    throw new ValidationException(message);
}
```

Use generic `<T> T raiseNotFound(String msg)` only when the compiler requires a return expression in `orElseThrow` chains.

## Error message style

* User-facing: clear, no stack traces in `detail`
* Log full exception in `@ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)` only
* Include entity type + id when helpful: `"Listing not found: " + id`

## Financial operations

When Payment Service lands, add:

* `IdempotencyConflictException` → 409
* `InsufficientFundsException` → 422
* `ComplianceBlockedException` → 422

Map in `GlobalExceptionHandler`; do not return generic 500 for business rejections.
